From **Vila do Corvo**, you can either take a taxi up the road to the Caldeirão rim, or walk uphill along the road. A traveler describes the taxi ride as about 10 minutes; another reports walking back from the crater area to the village jetty at roughly 6 km, so expect a substantial uphill walk if you go on foot. ([The Travel Fugitive](w1); [Where in the World Is Nina](w4))

The taxi is the easier option, especially if the weather is poor. Fog can completely hide the crater, so check conditions before making the trip; if walking, allow time and bring water. ([The Travel Fugitive](w1))

