Make the Buckskin Gulch detour at the **Buckskin–Paria confluence**: leave your pack at the junction if conditions and your judgment make that sensible, walk a short way **upstream into Buckskin Gulch**, then retrace your steps to the Paria and continue toward White House. That gives you a taste of the lower gulch without turning it into a much longer trip. [Bearfoot Theory’s Paria Canyon guide](w3) describes exploring the bottom of Buckskin from the confluence; on a White House start, the junction is about 7 miles down-canyon.

If you’re hiking from the Narrows toward White House, you’ll reach the junction before the White House end of the route. Check conditions before setting out: permits are required, and flash floods can make these narrow canyons dangerous.

